<title>FRANCE: Cetelem down, broker recommendation cut.</title>
<headline>Cetelem down, broker recommendation cut.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French consumer credit house Cetelem slid on the Paris Bourse on Friday, with Morgan Stanley confirming that it had lowered its recommendation on the stock to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot;.</p>
<p>A member of Morgan Stanley's research team said the move had been motivated by an already healthy performance from the stock in 1996.</p>
<p>The share was off 1.87 percent at 684 francs at 1413 GMT.</p>
</text>
